  "label": "the strained expression of holding back tears",
  "description": "The man's facial expression—furrowed brows, tight lips, and direct, intense gaze—visually conveys the physical and emotional strain of suppressing tears. This expression is not overtly crying but rather the internal struggle to contain an involuntary reaction, which is humorously linked to the act of cutting onions. The expression is exaggerated to match the absurdity of the situation described in the text.",
